      "notes": "Default .; byte-sorted one name per LF (no terminal columns). -a includes . and ..; -A omits those; -t modified descending, -S size descending, -r reverses final order; stable byte tie-break. -l names the owner and group through the platform account database (the decimal id when it has no name), with UTC timestamps, permissions and byte size; -h IEC units. -R bounded, no symlink recursion. -p appends / to directories; -i prefixes the inode and -s the allocated size in 1 KiB units (with -h, IEC), both right-aligned per listing, and -s adds the directory's total line; -n is -l with decimal uid and gid; -L describes link targets instead of links; -U keeps unsigned byte order (directory order is not deterministic); -c and -u select change and access time for -l, and sort by that time with -t or without -l; --group-directories-first lists directories before other entries; --color=never|auto prints plain names (output is never a terminal) and --color=always refuses; -G follows GNU: long listings omit the group column, and other listings are unchanged (BSD's color meaning does not apply). GNU, BSD and busybox spellings with one meaning are all accepted: -o is a long listing without the group and -g one without the owner; -f is -aU without long format; -k keeps -s in 1 KiB units (already the unit); -m separates names with ', ' and wraps before column 80; -H describes command-line links' targets; -P never follows links (the default).",
